oakMOSS: no endless interrupt from an I2C bus error.

A bus error (TWI status 0x00, an illegal level on SDA/SCL) left the controller's interrupt
flag set: the flag clear in that case sat after its goto and never ran, and the handler
re-enabled the interrupt unconditionally, so the same interrupt fired again for ever - a
hard lockup of the CPU taking it. On the XU20 this happens at every suspend with the touch
driver loaded: the display switches the panel rail (cldo2) off at the end of device suspend,
the touch controller on twi1 goes down with it, the lines collapse and the idle bus reports
a bus error (captured 2026-09-29: stat 0x00, ctl 0xc8, no transfer in flight). The board
froze on the way into sleep, or during resume when the interrupt was taken there.

Clear the flag in the bus-error case, re-enable the interrupt only while a transfer is in
flight (what the comment above that line already said), and treat an interrupt with no
transfer in flight as a stray: soft-reset the controller and leave the interrupt off -
sunxi_i2c_do_xfer resets the controller and enables it again for the next transfer.

--- a/lichee/linux-4.9/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-sunxi.c
+++ b/lichee/linux-4.9/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-sunxi.c
@@ -1692,9 +1692,8 @@
 		}
 	case 0x00: /* Bus error during master or slave mode due to illegal level condition */
 		err_code = 0xff;
+		twi_clear_irq_flag(base_addr);	/* oakMOSS: was dead code after the goto */
 		goto err_out;
-		twi_clear_irq_flag(base_addr);
-		break;
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_I2C_SLAVE)
 	case 0xB8:
@@ -1751,14 +1750,30 @@
 		/* disable irq */
 		twi_disable_irq(i2c->base_addr);
 
+		/*
+		 * oakMOSS: nothing in flight - a bus error with no transfer (the lines
+		 * collapsing when a device on the bus loses power, e.g. the XU20's touch
+		 * controller when the panel rail switches off at suspend). Reset the
+		 * controller and leave its interrupt off: sunxi_i2c_do_xfer resets it and
+		 * enables it again for the next transfer. The core process would have
+		 * dereferenced the NULL message here.
+		 */
+		if (i2c->status == I2C_XFER_IDLE) {
+			twi_soft_reset(i2c->base_addr, TWI_SRST_REG, TWI_SRST_SRST);
+			return IRQ_HANDLED;
+		}
+
 		/* twi core process */
 		sunxi_i2c_core_process(i2c);
 
 		/*
 		 * enable irq only when twi is transferring,
 		 * otherwise disable irq
+		 * (oakMOSS: the vendor code enabled it unconditionally, so a flag the
+		 * core process did not clear fired again for ever)
 		 */
-		twi_enable_irq(i2c->base_addr);
+		if (i2c->status != I2C_XFER_IDLE)
+			twi_enable_irq(i2c->base_addr);
 	}
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
